  "description": "Desperate for his father’s love, Un-Hyuk agrees to a suspicious proposal: spend two years in a rural village acting as a protective charm, and in return, inherit the family business. In the village, he encounters Tae-Moon, a mysterious young man rumored to be possessed by a ghost. Despite being ostracized by the villagers, Tae-Moon tirelessly seeks their approval. Haunted by memories of his own painful past, Un-Hyuk finds himself drawn to Tae-Moon’s plight and proposes a risky plan—one that could change both their fates and break the curse.\n\n(Source: Lezhin US)\n\n*Note: Includes six side story chapters.*",
